keywords:
  - numerical methods
  - engineering mathematics
  - Python
  - education
  - Jupyter
abstract: >-
  Readable from-scratch implementations of the numerical and symbolic methods engineers use - root
  finding, linear and nonlinear systems, interpolation, integration, differentiation, smoothing,
  curve fitting, ODEs, boundary-value problems, PDEs, Fourier analysis, optimisation and linear
  programming, Monte Carlo simulation and sparse solvers - validated against SciPy, exact solutions,
  NIST certified values and theoretical orders of convergence, with a 21-notebook course built on
  original engineering problems, real data files and worked solutions to all exercises.
